ndensed consolidated balance sheet. The Company also recognized a liability of $0.10 million related to remaining commission payments due, which is included within accrued expenses and other current liabilities in the condensed consolidated balance sheet as of June 30, 2026.","context":"For the three and six months ended June 30, 2026, the Company recognized net charges related to the sale of the Judith Ripka brand (consisting of impairment charges to write-down the carrying value of the Judith Ripka trademarks prior to their sale, and costs of the sale) of $0.04 million and $0.10 million, respectively.","section":"Segment Reporting Information","block":128,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-096016","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001083220","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083220/000110465926096016/xelb-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/65e29c00978462c00273e3a5070ec5802c36586efb67c97e174cff7b284f5c0a.bin","sha256":"65e29c00978462c00273e3a5070ec5802c36586efb67c97e174cff7b284f5c0a"}},{"id":"e9057ef65fb11cd908145e73d46f8f088ce27f2c4488c4215d151762ecf9859a","quote":"Longaberger Licensing, LLC Variable Interest Entity","context":"Upon the sale of the Judith Ripka brand, the Company recognized $0.64 million of earn-out consideration receivable from the Buyer, based on the Company’s estimate of probable future payments to be received under the terms of the asset purchase agreement; as of June 30, 2026, $0.14 million of this amount was recorded within prepaid expenses and other current assets in the condensed consolidated balance sheet, and $0.50 million was recorded within other assets (non-current) in the condensed consolidated balance sheet. The Company also recognized a liability of $0.10 million related to remaining commission payments due, which is included within accrued expenses and other current liabilities in the condensed consolidated balance sheet as of June 30, 2026.","section":"Segment Reporting Information","block":129,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-096016","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001083220","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083220/000110465926096016/xelb-20260630x10q.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/65e29c00978462c00273e3a5070ec5802c36586efb67c97e174cff7b284f5c0a.bin","sha256":"65e29c00978462c00273e3a5070ec5802c36586efb67c97e174cff7b284f5c0a"}},{"id":"93f2f812a7e4e7eca5369224cd9437455eb9b2ec11cdd6422becf114ffa1d7b3","quote":"Since 2019, Xcel has been party to a limited liability company agreement with a subsidiary of Hilco Global related to Longaberger Licensing, LLC (“LL”). Hilco Global is the sole Class A Member of LL, and Xcel is the sole Class B Member of LL (each individually a “Member”). Each Member holds a 50% equity ownership interest in LL; however, based on an analysis of the contractual terms and rights contained in the LLC agreement and related agreements, the Company has previously determined that under the applicable accounting standards, LL is a variable interest entity and the Company has effective control over LL. Therefore, as the primary beneficiary, the Company has consolidated LL since 2019, and has recognized the assets, liabilities, revenues, and expenses of LL as part of its consolidated financial statements, along with a noncontrolling interest which represents Hilco Global’s 50% ownership share in LL.","context":"Longaberger Licensing, LLC Variable Interest Entity","section":"Segment Reporting Information","block":130,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-096016","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001083220","url":"https://ww